{
  "schema_version": "creib.mini.manifest.v1",
  "manifest_id": "mini.experiment.r1.s2-source-adversary",
  "problem": "The checks under test are the conformance harness's own functions, shown to you as source: how it recovers a JSON object from a reply, whether it had to recover it from prose, its response verdict, its refusal-phrase check, and its grounding matcher. The question for every seat: is there a rewrite of an input under which a check's answer ought to change and does not, or changes where nobody would expect it to? The executor runs the check by machine on what you give it and records what its answer did; nothing here decides anything, the record shows what moved.",
  "cycles": {
    "max_cycles": 3
  },
  "port_types": [
    {
      "port_type": "kernel_source",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.kernel-source.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies",
        "header": "The source of the checks"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "pair_proposals",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.pair-proposal.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies_and_commitments",
        "header": "Proposals so far"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "pair_executions",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.pair-execution.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies_and_commitments",
        "header": "Executions"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "criticisms",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.criticism.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies",
        "header": "Criticisms"
      }
    },
    {
      "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
      "draws_from": {
        "artifact_kinds": [
          "mini.verdict.v1"
        ]
      },
      "render": {
        "rule": "list_bodies_and_commitments",
        "header": "Verdicts so far"
      }
    }
  ],
  "kinds": [
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.kernel-source.v1",
      "title": "Source",
      "input_ports": [],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.kernel-source.v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-proposal.v1",
      "title": "Proposal",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "problem",
          "port_type": "problem",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "source",
          "port_type": "kernel_source",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "earlier",
          "port_type": "pair_proposals",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "verdicts",
          "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "criticisms",
          "port_type": "criticisms",
          "window": "previous_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.pair-proposal.v1"
      },
      "instruction": "Read the source closely. Find a place where the implementation departs from the rule its docstring states, or where two inputs a person would treat alike get different answers, or where inputs a person would treat differently get the same answer. Write the pair that shows it: an input and a rewritten input that differ in exactly that respect, and expect per the DOCSTRING's stated rule, not per what you think the code will do; the executor will tell us which. Any kernel in the registry; a JSON object reply, a prose reply, or a grounding object {value, span, document} as the kernel needs. Prefer the recovery and grounding kernels, and cases involving fences, prose inside fences, braces inside string values, repeated keys, quotation marks, and whitespace. The commitments are a STRING whose content is JSON of the form {\"kernel\": \"<id>\", \"input\": \"<the input text>\", \"rewritten\": \"<your rewritten text>\", \"expect\": \"moves\" or \"unchanged\", \"rewrite\": \"<one sentence naming what you changed>\"}. The input and the rewritten text are instances written out in full, never descriptions. Do not repeat a pair shown among the earlier proposals.",
      "format": {
        "commitments": {
          "all_of": [
            {
              "check": "json_schema",
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "kernel",
                  "input",
                  "rewritten",
                  "expect",
                  "rewrite"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "kernel": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "pattern": "^conformance\\.kernel\\."
                  },
                  "input": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  "rewritten": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 1
                  },
                  "expect": {
                    "enum": [
                      "moves",
                      "unchanged"
                    ]
                  },
                  "rewrite": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "minLength": 3
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "commitment_call": "single"
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-execution.v1",
      "title": "Execution",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "proposals",
          "port_type": "pair_proposals",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.pair-execution.v1"
      }
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.criticism.v1",
      "title": "Criticism",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "problem",
          "port_type": "problem",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "source",
          "port_type": "kernel_source",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "proposals",
          "port_type": "pair_proposals",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "executions",
          "port_type": "pair_executions",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.criticism.v1"
      },
      "instruction": "Do not propose. Read this cycle's executions beside the proposals: say which expectations held, which failed, and why, reading the source; say which failures matter, which are trivial, and what a proposer should try next. Cite blocks by id."
    },
    {
      "kind_id": "mini.verdict.v1",
      "title": "Verdict",
      "input_ports": [
        {
          "port_id": "executions",
          "port_type": "pair_executions",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "criticisms",
          "port_type": "criticisms",
          "window": "this_cycle"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "verdicts",
          "port_type": "earlier_verdicts",
          "window": "all"
        },
        {
          "port_id": "catalogue",
          "port_type": "evidence_legend",
          "window": "all",
          "params": {
            "tiers": [
              "evidence"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "output_port": {
        "port_id": "out",
        "produces_kind": "mini.verdict.v1"
      },
      "format": {
        "commitments": {
          "all_of": [
            {
              "check": "json_schema",
              "schema": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": [
                  "verdicts"
                ],
                "properties": {
                  "verdicts": {
                    "type": "array",
                    "items": {
                      "type": "object",
                      "required": [
                        "proposal",
                        "executed",
                        "catalogued",
                        "standing"
                      ],
                      "properties": {
                        "proposal": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "kernel": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "transform": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "executed": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "expected": {
                          "type": "string"
                        },
                        "catalogued": {
                          "type": "boolean"
                        },
                        "same_input": {
                          "type": [
                            "boolean",
                            "null"
                          ]
                        },
                        "standing": {
                          "enum": [
                            "candidate point",
                            "defect",
                            "rejected"
                          ]
                        },
                        "column": {
                          "enum": [
                            "moves",
                            "unchanged",
                            null
                          ]
                        }
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "stages": [
    {
      "stage_id": "source",
      "kind_id": "mini.kernel-source.v1",
      "seat": "machine",
      "ports": []
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "propose-1",
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-proposal.v1",
      "ports": [
        "problem",
        "source",
        "earlier",
        "verdicts",
        "criticisms",
        "catalogue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "propose-2",
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-proposal.v1",
      "ports": [
        "problem",
        "source",
        "earlier",
        "verdicts",
        "criticisms",
        "catalogue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "execute",
      "kind_id": "mini.pair-execution.v1",
      "seat": "machine",
      "ports": [
        "proposals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "criticise",
      "kind_id": "mini.criticism.v1",
      "ports": [
        "problem",
        "source",
        "proposals",
        "executions",
        "catalogue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "verdict",
      "kind_id": "mini.verdict.v1",
      "seat": "machine",
      "ports": [
        "executions",
        "criticisms",
        "verdicts",
        "catalogue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "stage_id": "end",
      "end": true
    }
  ],
  "sources": [
    {
      "source_id": "catalogue",
      "path": "catalogue.json"
    },
    {
      "source_id": "registry",
      "path": "registry.txt"
    }
  ]
}
